            <ArticleTitle>Follicular bronchiolitis in primary ciliary dyskinesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>294-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4066/AMJ.2014.2102</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ciliary dysfunction in primary ciliary dyskinesia (PCD) may be associated with bronchiolitis. Diffuse bronchiolitis has been reported in a subset of PCD patients who have Kartagener's syndrome in Japan. We report a case of follicular bronchiolitis (FB) in a case of PCD presenting with recurrent episodes of cough, dyspnea, and bronchiectasis. This may motivate researchers to study rarer variants and presentations in PCD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
